1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:16,638
All fifty questions from topics 6–10 with model answers — exactly the way the examiner asks. Plus the twelve most important phrases and five mistakes that cost people points. Get ready and answer out loud!

2
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:29,315
How does the task work? The examiner chooses two topics and asks four questions on each. That is eight questions in total, and each good answer gets one point.

3
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:41,969
You know the topics in advance, but not the questions. So now we will go through all ten questions of each topic. Answer with a full sentence, ideally two, and listen to the tense.

4
00:00:42,867 --> 00:00:46,731
Topic 6: Work. Ten questions.

5
00:00:47,233 --> 00:00:48,384
Where do you work?

6
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:57,474
I work in a warehouse in Kralupy.

7
00:00:58,567 --> 00:01:00,456
What do you do at work every day?

8
00:01:07,767 --> 00:01:11,289
Every day I load and unload goods and check boxes.

9
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,750
When do you start and finish work?

10
00:01:22,067 --> 00:01:24,790
I start at six in the morning and finish at two in the afternoon.

11
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,437
How do you get to work?

12
00:01:34,733 --> 00:01:37,625
I drive to work, it's about ten minutes.

13
00:01:38,733 --> 00:01:40,214
Do you like your job?

14
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:51,770
I like my job because I have good colleagues, but it's quite hard.

15
00:01:52,867 --> 00:01:54,335
Do you speak Czech at work?

16
00:02:01,633 --> 00:02:06,156
Yes, I speak Czech with my boss and sometimes Ukrainian with colleagues.

17
00:02:07,267 --> 00:02:08,845
What job did you do before?

18
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:18,255
I used to work as a taxi driver.

19
00:02:19,367 --> 00:02:21,079
How did you find this job?

20
00:02:28,367 --> 00:02:30,999
I found this job online through an agency.

21
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:34,538
How many days of holiday will you have this year?

22
00:02:41,833 --> 00:02:44,143
This year I'll have twenty days of holiday.

23
00:02:45,233 --> 00:02:47,440
What job would you like to do in five years?

24
00:02:54,733 --> 00:02:57,930
In five years I'd like to work in an office as an accountant.

25
00:02:59,033 --> 00:03:03,581
Topic 7: School and education. Ten questions.

26
00:03:04,067 --> 00:03:05,577
What school did you attend?

27
00:03:12,867 --> 00:03:16,266
I finished secondary school and then studied economics at university.

28
00:03:17,367 --> 00:03:18,873
What did you study?

29
00:03:26,167 --> 00:03:28,484
I studied economics and accounting.

30
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,829
Which subject did you like at school?

31
00:03:39,133 --> 00:03:41,895
At school I liked maths and geography.

32
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,836
How long did you go to school?

33
00:03:52,133 --> 00:03:55,394
I went to school for eleven years and to university for five.

34
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,070
Do your children go to school?

35
00:04:05,367 --> 00:04:09,097
Yes, my son goes to primary school, he's in year three.

36
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:12,301
How far is the school from your flat?

37
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:22,408
The school is close, about ten minutes on foot.

38
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,811
What are you learning now?

39
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:35,098
I'm learning Czech now, I go to a course twice a week.

40
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:37,863
How do your children learn Czech?

41
00:04:45,167 --> 00:04:48,378
The children learn Czech at school and speak Czech with friends.

42
00:04:49,467 --> 00:04:51,079
Will you study anything else?

43
00:04:58,367 --> 00:05:01,191
Yes, next year I'll do an accounting course.

44
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,846
What would you like to study if you had time?

45
00:05:12,133 --> 00:05:15,532
If I had time, I would study computers and programming.

46
00:05:16,633 --> 00:05:20,975
Topic 8: The Czech language. Ten questions.

47
00:05:21,467 --> 00:05:23,181
How long have you been learning Czech?

48
00:05:30,467 --> 00:05:32,276
I've been learning Czech for about two years.

49
00:05:33,367 --> 00:05:34,799
How did you learn Czech?

50
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:45,667
I learned on a course, from an app on my phone and from TV.

51
00:05:46,767 --> 00:05:48,877
Where do you speak Czech most often?

52
00:05:56,167 --> 00:05:58,828
I speak Czech most often at work and in shops.

53
00:05:59,933 --> 00:06:01,558
Is Czech difficult for you?

54
00:06:08,867 --> 00:06:12,146
Czech is difficult, especially the grammar and the pronunciation of ř.

55
00:06:13,233 --> 00:06:15,694
What is the hardest thing in Czech for you?

56
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,144
The hardest for me are the cases and long vowels.

57
00:06:27,233 --> 00:06:28,269
Do you read in Czech?

58
00:06:35,567 --> 00:06:39,459
Yes, I read news online and sometimes short children's books.

59
00:06:40,567 --> 00:06:42,542
Do you watch Czech TV?

60
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:53,093
Yes, in the evening I watch Czech news and series.

61
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,420
Why are you learning Czech?

62
00:07:02,733 --> 00:07:06,697
I'm learning Czech because I live here and want permanent residence.

63
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:09,273
How will you keep learning?

64
00:07:16,567 --> 00:07:19,458
I'll go to a course and talk more with Czech colleagues.

65
00:07:20,567 --> 00:07:23,859
What would you advise someone who is starting Czech?

66
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:33,897
I'd advise them to speak every day, even if they make mistakes.

67
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,798
Topic 9: Daily routine. Ten questions.

68
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,694
What time do you get up?

69
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,489
On weekdays I get up at five in the morning.

70
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,881
What do you do in the morning?

71
00:08:00,167 --> 00:08:04,323
In the morning I wash, get dressed, have breakfast and go to work.

72
00:08:05,433 --> 00:08:06,505
What do you have for breakfast?

73
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:16,316
For breakfast I eat bread with cheese and drink coffee.

74
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,633
Where do you have lunch?

75
00:08:25,933 --> 00:08:29,817
I have lunch in the canteen at work, usually soup and a main course.

76
00:08:30,933 --> 00:08:32,361
What do you do in the afternoon?

77
00:08:39,667 --> 00:08:42,243
In the afternoon I pick up my son from school and do the shopping.

78
00:08:43,333 --> 00:08:44,759
What do you do in the evening?

79
00:08:52,067 --> 00:08:55,852
In the evening I cook dinner, watch TV and study Czech.

80
00:08:56,967 --> 00:08:58,396
What time do you go to bed?

81
00:09:05,700 --> 00:09:07,984
I go to bed at about ten in the evening.

82
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,790
What did you do yesterday evening?

83
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:21,144
Yesterday evening I cooked soup and then read a book.

84
00:09:22,233 --> 00:09:23,911
What will you do tomorrow morning?

85
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:33,827
Tomorrow morning I'll go to the doctor and then to work.

86
00:09:34,933 --> 00:09:37,237
How would you like to change your day?

87
00:09:44,533 --> 00:09:46,853
I'd like to have more time for sport and for my family.

88
00:09:47,967 --> 00:09:52,062
Topic 10: The weekend. Ten questions.

89
00:09:52,567 --> 00:09:54,348
What do you usually do at the weekend?

90
00:10:01,633 --> 00:10:05,278
At the weekend I rest, tidy up and go out with my family.

91
00:10:06,367 --> 00:10:07,960
Do you sometimes work at the weekend?

92
00:10:15,267 --> 00:10:18,087
Sometimes I work on Saturday, but I have Sundays off.

93
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,801
When do you get up on Saturday?

94
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:30,969
On Saturday I get up later, at about eight.

95
00:10:32,067 --> 00:10:33,389
Where do you go at the weekend?

96
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:45,255
At the weekend we go to the park, the swimming pool or the shopping centre.

97
00:10:46,367 --> 00:10:47,827
Who do you spend the weekend with?

98
00:10:55,133 --> 00:10:58,071
I spend the weekend mostly with my family and sometimes with friends.

99
00:10:59,167 --> 00:11:00,779
What did you do last weekend?

100
00:11:08,067 --> 00:11:10,906
Last weekend we went on a trip to Karlštejn Castle.

101
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,686
What was your best weekend?

102
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,133
The best weekend was last summer when we were at a lake.

103
00:11:25,233 --> 00:11:26,688
What will you do this weekend?

104
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,120
This weekend I'll be at home because I have to clean and cook.

105
00:11:38,233 --> 00:11:39,846
Where will you go next weekend?

106
00:11:47,133 --> 00:11:49,497
Next weekend we'll go to see friends in Brno.

107
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:52,946
How would you like to spend an ideal weekend?

108
00:12:00,233 --> 00:12:03,222
I'd like to spend an ideal weekend in the mountains without a phone.

109
00:12:04,333 --> 00:12:09,040
Now the twelve most important phrases. Listen and repeat out loud.

110
00:12:09,733 --> 00:12:11,587
My name is Oleh Kovalenko.

111
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:17,100
I am from Ukraine, from Kharkiv.

112
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:22,333
I live in Kralupy nad Vltavou.

113
00:12:25,533 --> 00:12:27,033
I have been in Czechia for five years.

114
00:12:30,233 --> 00:12:31,433
I work in a warehouse.

115
00:12:34,633 --> 00:12:36,428
I have a wife and two sons.

116
00:12:39,633 --> 00:12:41,965
In my free time I like going for walks.

117
00:12:45,167 --> 00:12:47,729
I like the flat because it is bright.

118
00:12:50,933 --> 00:12:52,867
Last Saturday I was at the market.

119
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:57,833
Next summer we will go to the sea.

120
00:13:01,033 --> 00:13:03,300
In five years I would like to have a better job.

121
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:08,700
I think I am calm and friendly.

122
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,958
Five typical mistakes that cost people points.

123
00:13:18,167 --> 00:13:24,392
Correct: Bydlím v Kralupech nad Vltavou. Answer with a full sentence, not one word.

124
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:33,709
Correct: Jsem z Ukrajiny. After the preposition z we use the 2nd case: z Ukrajiny, z Kyjeva.

125
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:44,334
Correct: Bydlím v Praze. After the preposition v we use the 6th case: v Praze, v Brně.

126
00:13:48,033 --> 00:13:54,064
Correct: Je mi čtyřicet let. This is how we say age: je mi … let.

127
00:13:57,767 --> 00:14:05,519
Correct: Rodiče jsem naposledy viděl loni v létě. The question is in the past tense, so the answer must be too.

128
00:14:06,733 --> 00:14:28,429
Summary. First: answer with a full sentence, ideally two. Second: listen to the tense of the question and answer in the same tense. Third: watch the cases — z Ukrajiny, v Praze. And fourth: be specific — numbers, places, names.

129
00:14:29,633 --> 00:14:38,878
